# HSM collector conformance v1 — table sensors (#1846, ADR-0021 points 5-7).
#
# The managed collector implements them (4.1.0); the native collector gets them with step 6 (#1848): its driver
# marks every verb below CONFORMANCE-UNSUPPORTED (#1848) and does not register this fixture until then.
#
# Rows are compared decoded, never as bytes: two zstd libraries may compress the same block to different bytes.
# The table tick never runs on its own in a driver: table_tick runs one, and waits for the registration and the
# delivery it starts. Times are milliseconds since 1970-01-01 UTC.
#
# New verbs:
# create_collector_without_table_transport                a collector whose sender cannot carry tables
# create_table_sensor|path|columns                        under the collector identity (computer/module), as every sensor;
#                                                         columns: name:type pairs, comma-separated, type double or int64,
#                                                         "none" for no column; the time column is implicit and first
# create_table_sensor_at_product|path|columns             the same at the product root
# expect_create_table_sensor_rejected|path|columns        the call itself is refused (managed: ArgumentException)
# add_table_row|path|time_ms|v1|v2...                     one row; token:null for a cell without a value
# add_table_rows|path|count|start_ms                      count rows at once: row r has the time start_ms + r and the
#                                                         value r in every column
# table_tick                                              one table tick
# table_server_refuse_registration|path|reason            the server refuses the registration of path, with reason
# table_server_fail_registrations|count                   the next count registration requests get no answer
# table_server_down / table_server_up                     while down, no block gets an answer
# table_server_frame_limit|bytes                          the largest frame the table connection takes, header included
# table_server_answer_next|outcome                        the next block is answered: stored, duplicate, all_refused,
#                                                         invalid (400), not_delivered (503)
# table_server_refuse_table_next|path|reason              the next block is stored with the table of path refused
# expect_table_add_results|digits                         the add verbs so far, in order: 1 taken, 0 dropped
# expect_table_path|path|full_path                        the path the sensor is registered and named under
# expect_table_state|path|state                           pending, registered, refused or unavailable
# expect_table_rows_accepted|path|count / expect_table_rows_dropped|path|count   the sensor's own counters
# expect_table_registration_count|count                   table registration requests so far
# expect_table_registration_size|index|count              request index carries count registrations, all of tables
# expect_table_registration|index|path|columns            request index registers path with these columns, time first
# expect_table_blocks|count                               blocks stored so far
# expect_table_block_attempts|count                       blocks put so far, answered or not
# expect_table_block_tables|index|count                   stored block index holds count tables
# expect_table_blocks_within|bytes                        every frame put (block + 40-byte header) is within bytes
# expect_table_sequences|s0,s1,...                        the producer sequences of every put, in order; one producer
# expect_table_sequences_increasing                       every put repeats or exceeds the sequence before; one producer
# expect_table_rows|path|count                            rows of path stored (refused tables do not count)
# expect_table_row|path|index|time_ms|v1|v2...            the index-th stored row of path

